    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "O HARE INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT\nCHICAGO ILL.",
      "O HARE\nINTERNATIONAL AIRPORT\nPLACE\nSTAMP\nHERE\nCHICAGO, ILL.\nCOPYRIGHT MCMLXXVI BY CURT TEICH \u0026 CO., CHICAGO, U.S.A.",
      "UNITED\nINTERNATIONAL CUSTOMS\nTICKET COUNTERS AND BAGGAGE CHECK-IN AREA\nO'HARE AT NIGHT\nUNITED",
      "O'HARE INT'L. AIRPORT\nINTERNATIONAL TERMINAL",
      "Greetings from\nDISTRIBUTED BY JOBOUL PUBLISHING CO.. EvANSTON. ILLINOI\nCURTEICHCOLOR®) 3-D NATURAL COLOR REPRODUCTIONS (REG. U. S. A. PAT. OFF.)\nD-19816\nCROSSROADS OF THE WORLD\nIt is virtually impossible to imagine the enor-\nmous size of Chicago O'Hare International\nAirport, nor the volume of traffic and passen-\ngers handled.\nO'Hare is by far the busiest airport in the\nworld. Approximately fifteen million passen-\ngers and well over a half million flights are\nhanded annually.\nDaily flights alone are equivalent to half the\nentire jet airline fleet of the whole world.\nOnly the most modern facilities could cope\nwith this enormous traffic. O'Hare offers all\nconveniences, including world-famous restau-\nrants that will serve as many as fifteen hun-\ndred people at one time.\nThere is direct service available to almost\nevery\nmajor city in the world.\nFrom any\npoint of view, Chicago is truly the air capitai\nof the world.\nTHE FLAGS AT O'HARE\nAERIAL VIEW\nCONTROL TOWER AND LOADING RAMPS",
      "NEWS - STAND\nNEWS STAND AND CONCOURSE\nRESTAURANT ROTUNDA\nENTRANCE HIGHWAY AND PLANE OVERPASS\nCzare Airport\nTERMINAL AND INTERIORS"
    ],
